course: dictionary
lesson: 3871
title: A name with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word that starts with a capital letter is often a name. Names are proper nouns: they name one special person, place or thing. «Benjamin Franklin» is one real man, so the capital letters tell you that Franklin is a name.
explain: Franklin is a name, but it is also an old word from history. In old England, a franklin was a free man who owned land but was not a lord or a knight. Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence is about a person, a place or a voyage, it is probably the name. If it talks about the Middle Ages or Chaucer, it may be the old word.
explain: Use the context to decide. «Franklin the Turtle» is a character in children's books, so Franklin is a name there too. «The Franklin expedition» was a lost voyage to the Arctic, so Franklin names a voyage. A quick check: swap in another name, like «Sam the Turtle». If it still makes sense, Franklin is a name.
fact: Franklin is a proper noun when it is a name, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Benjamin Franklin» was one of the founders of the United States, and he invented the lightning rod.
fact: «Benjamin Franklin» reported his kite experiment in 1752, and some historians doubt it happened as told.
fact: «Franklin» is also the name of many towns in the United States.
fact: In old England, a franklin was a free man who owned land but was not a lord or a knight.
exercise: In «Benjamin Franklin's kite experiment», is Franklin a name? | Yes, it means a storm | No, it means a free man who owns land | No, it is a type of kite | *Yes, it is the name of a man
exercise: «Franklin the Turtle» is in many children's books. What is Franklin here? | *A name for a character | A type of ship | A free man who owned land | A lightning rod
exercise: «Benjamin Franklin invented the lightning rod.» What did he invent? | A new kind of ship | A kite made of silk | A map of the Arctic | *A lightning rod
test: In old England, what was a franklin? | A lord who ruled a castle | *A free man who owned land, but was not a lord or a knight | A kind of kite | A ship sailing to the Arctic
test: Why does Franklin start with a capital letter in «Benjamin Franklin»? | Because it is the name of a place | Because it is a long word | Because it starts a sentence | *Because it is the name of one special person
exam: In «a franklin was a free man who owned land», what does franklin mean? | A name for a ship | *An old word for a free man who owned land | A name for a turtle | A kind of lightning rod
